<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tomislavgrad</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Duvno</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tomislavgrad is a town in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herzegovina">Herzegovina</a>, on the Duvno plain. Near it lay <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delminium">Delminium</a>, the stronghold of the Delmatae, and later a Roman town. Long known as Duvno, it was renamed in 1925 for King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomislav-of-croatia">Tomislav of Croatia</a>, who according to tradition was crowned in the area in 925.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tomislavgrad.jpg" alt="Tomislavgrad" width="320" height="154" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dulmiensis · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Municipality_building_in_Tomislavgrad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
